We already set the permissions for the $JENKINS_HOME earlier in the DockerfileTemplate - see line 28 - I think the problem is that we do that before useradd which is actually acting on the existing $JENKINS_HOME folder which might be the problem here: useradd -l -m on an existing directory can reset ownership/permissions on that directory
If u move the chown command after useradd it will get persisted for the later steps, e.g.:

RUN mkdir -p $JENKINS_HOME \
  && groupadd -g ${gid} ${group} \
  && useradd -N -d "$JENKINS_HOME" -u ${uid} -g ${gid} -l -m -s /bin/bash ${user} \
  && chown -R ${uid}:${gid} $JENKINS_HOME


